{{define "content"}}
<vox-hero eyebrow="Classification" heading="Decide what runs where" data-i18n-attr="heading,eyebrow">
  <p data-i18n>
    Node groups match on the facts your nodes already report and hand
    openvox-server the answer over the ENC contract it expects.
  </p>
</vox-hero>

<section class="site-section">
  <h2 class="vox-ts-xxl" data-i18n>Groups that match real nodes</h2>
  <div class="vox-prose">
    <p data-i18n-html>
      Build a rule from facts &mdash; <code>os.family = Debian</code>,
      <code>role = web</code> &mdash; and the console tells you how many
      nodes it matches right now. A rule that catches nothing is obvious
      immediately, instead of at the next Puppet run.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{{screenshot "groups-list"}}

<section class="site-section">
  <h2 class="vox-ts-xxl" data-i18n>Precedence you can read off the page</h2>
  <div class="vox-prose">
    <p data-i18n>
      Groups form a tree, and a group only ever contains nodes its
      parent does. When several groups apply to a node, a group always
      wins over the groups above it, and an explicit priority decides
      between the rest. If that ever lets a child override a parent with
      a higher priority, the console says so on the group instead of
      leaving you to work it out.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<vox-step-indicator>
  <vox-step>A node asks for its catalog</vox-step>
  <vox-step>openvox-server asks the console what applies</vox-step>
  <vox-step>Matching groups merge, child over parent</vox-step>
  <vox-step>Classes, parameters and environment come back</vox-step>
</vox-step-indicator>

<vox-callout variant="warning" heading="Rules match on reported facts" data-i18n-attr="heading">
  <p data-i18n>
    A node that has never checked in has no facts yet, so no fact-based
    rule can match it. It is still in All Nodes, and can be pinned to a
    group directly beneath it if it needs more before its first run.
  </p>
</vox-callout>
{{end}}
